x86_64-linux  cxx1 emits the C1 form of B<int>::Box's constructor beside the C2 where clang emits only the C2 it calls - the inline-constructor difference implicit-move.nonames records. A nested class of a class template cannot have its constructor written out of line here, which is how the other two classes in the case avoid it. x86_64-windows and arm64-darwin agree on every name.
